  "body": "Deadline sale: Closes on Thursday 19 November 2026 at 2:00PM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nWake to a spectacular sunrise over Rangitoto Island, with phenomenal city and sea views from your kitchen, living area and balcony. The largest home in the collection offers approx. 182m² of gross building area on a generous 232m² freehold site, in an established, leafy pocket of central Torbay filled with charm and birdsong. \r\n\r\nDesigned for teenagers or extended family wanting space and privacy, the home offers four bedrooms, three bathrooms and a downstairs study that could serve as a fifth bedroom.\r\nYour home enjoys sea views, from sweeping panoramas across the Hauraki Gulf to a peaceful outlook over treetops to the water.\r\n\r\nThe upstairs living area features high stud ceilings, designer skylights and oversized windows, creating a bright, spacious setting for everyday family life. A high-spec kitchen with an island bench connects with the open-plan living area, where light beach-toned flooring adds to the coastal feel. Sliding out to the sunny balcony, it’s the perfect spot for your first coffee of the day. \r\n\r\nDownstairs is all about flexibility, with generous bedrooms and bathrooms providing privacy for teenagers or visiting guests, space to work from home, and a private deck and garden to enjoy. An internal access double garage, generous off-street parking and an extra-wide driveway make coming home easy, while a 10-Year Master Build Guarantee brings lasting peace of mind.\r\n\r\nYou can literally stroll to your local shops and cafés, swim and picnic at Long Bay Regional Park, launch your boat or kayak just down the road at Waiake Beach, even learn to sail at the Torbay Sailing Club. Zoned for Torbay School, Northcross Intermediate and Long Bay College. \r\n\r\nViews like this rarely come with a brand-new home, and the seller has given clear instructions to sell. Enquire today and secure your new home this summer!",
